this is curtin davina reading for kevin  kenizevic  with 2016's monster hunter stories for  the 3ds capcom transformed its real-time  strategy monster hunting series  into something dramatically different a  colorful  turn-based monster collecting rpg  despite the stark change in tone and  gameplay  stories offered a new perspective on the  monster hunter universe  making it an enjoyable alternative to  the mainline series  its follow-up monster hunter stories 2  wings of ruin very much follows  the template that the original 3ds game  set and despite some repetitive elements  it's another solid spinoff for the  [Music]  franchise  like its predecessor monster hunter  stories 2 trades monster slaying  for monster collecting rather than  casting you in the role of a hunter the  game puts you in the boots of a fledging  writer  someone who is able to form bonds with  monsters and fight alongside them while  you'll still need to hunt down plenty of  monsters during your journey  you'll spend most of your time exploring  dens and collecting new  monster companions that you can raise  and take into battle  this makes monster hunter stories 2  closer to pokemon than to a traditional  monster hunter title but the game plays  out much differently  than nintendo's monster catching series  foremost is the way you collect monsters  rather than taming wild ones you obtain  new monsters by entering monster dens  and gathering their eggs these crop up  randomly each time you set out into the  overworld and primarily come in  two varieties standard dens and golden  rare dens that typically obtain better  eggs  regardless of their type the dens  themselves are all rudimentary in terms  of their layouts  beyond some occasional branching  pathways which usually just lead to  optional treasures  there are no real environmental puzzles  to solve  so they're not particularly compelling  to explore on their own  despite this the allure of discovering  new kinds of eggs  never grows old and makes trekking  through dens  worthwhile especially as you progress  through the story  and begin encountering cooler monsters  in addition to regular monster duns  each major area in the game also  features a handful of larger dungeons  called  everdads these are much more  labyrinth-like than standard dens and  house some unique treasures such as  rare eggs and bottle caps which can be  exchanged for special items and upgrades  like  increased storage space for your  monsters these upgrades make bottle caps  among the most  valuable commodities in the game but  they're not as satisfying to find  like regular dens aberdens don't offer  much variety so they end up feeling  samey and  aren't all enjoyable to navigate and no  thanks to their whining pathways you'll  often  hit multiple dead ends before you  eventually locate the monster nest which  makes everton's more of a chore to  explore than regular dents  after you've obtained an egg you can  take it back to the stables and hatch a  new monster  depending on the egg's rarity and weight  the monster you obtain will boast  different genes which  determines what skills and attacks it  will be able to use during the battle  these genes are crucial if you hope to  get the most out of your monstem and  they become a sort of  mini-game unto themselves if you align  three jeans of the same color you'll  achieve a bingo  bonus which will power up your mazda  even further you can also pass genes  between monsters through a process  called  rite of channeling this offers a  pleasing amount of flexibility in  customizing your monste's skills and  feels rewarding to devise  new combinations  your monsies primarily come in use in  battle unlike the mainline series  encounters and monster hunter stories  too  are turn-based while there are elemental  weaknesses and advantages to consider  battles revolve around three different  types of attacks  power speed and technical each type has  an advantage  over another speed bests power power  beats technical  and technical overcome speed the crux of  the battles then  become figuring out which type of attack  the enemy monster will use  and swapping in the right monster to  counter it it's a simple yet  satisfying system and the game keeps it  fresh by introducing new kinds of  monsters with different attack patterns  the weapons you use are also crucial to  combat  weapons like monsters fall into three  varieties  slash pierce and blunt which lends  itself an additional layer of strategy  different parts of a monster are  susceptible to a particular type of  weapon  so you'll need to swap out weapons  frequently during the course of a battle  and target specific parts to deal the  most damage  attack apart enough times and you will  eventually break it causing the monster  to drop  a material and topple over while a  monster is prone on the ground each  attack will deal critical  damage and you can even halt some  monsters from unleashing their strongest  attacks  by breaking a specific part of their  body these wrinkles make battles feel  consistently enjoyable  and the game boasts some nice quality of  life features such as the ability to  fast forward animations and even  end battles against lower level foes  immediately to mitigate the grind  beyond their in-battle abilities each  monster can also perform a certain  action while you ride them out in the  field  which will help you reach some otherwise  inaccessible areas  the yeon kudku for instance can smash  rocks that are blocking the path  however these writing actions are  underutilized during the maid adventure  which is disappointing  rather than opening up new paths to  explore these skills are typically used  to reach  out of the way treasure chests whose  contents are  often underwhelming as a result the  skills used in the field are  largely unnecessary and don't really add  anything to the experience  the weakest element in monster hunter  stories 2 is  ironically its story while the narrative  is certainly more involved than a  traditional monster hunter game  it largely stays within jrpg tropes and  is predictable  as a result  the story also skews toward a younger  audience as evidenced by  navarro your cartoonish wise cracking  feline companion  from here on out we're gonna be partners  and i'll do it all totally free of  charge  since your avatar never speaks navarro  takes up most of the dialogue  and he frequently straddles the line  between cute and  annoying that said the story does broach  some themes that the mainline series  never explores such as the seemingly  incompatible world views  of hunters and writers and it's filled  with humorous  and touching moments overall monster  hunter stories 2  wings of ruin is an enjoyable monster  hunter spin-off and an all-around  solid jrpg particularly if you enjoy  games like pokemon while the title  retains some of the series hallmark  elements  its emphasis on monster collecting and  its fun turn based battle system  make it a different experience than  monster hunter rise one  that even those who've struggled to get  into the proper monster hunter series  can enjoy  [Music]  you
 

